[{:db/id "q-127920/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "02994221-4439-5e58-8012-b40a13656205" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127920/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "633bc8c3-c64a-58e0-b977-0356c58fe505" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127920/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "996c1082-2d0d-5dde-846e-ad9988faf98e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127920/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "cc0a6007-9114-5231-8f50-5293c308332b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127920/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "cbb8f0b6-f8a1-574f-b443-0a959cba67bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127920/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f09112c9-c4c2-58e3-aa6c-7acb4f392b39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127920/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-127920/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-127920/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-127920/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-127920/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-127920/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127920" :question/id #uuid "204b8021-c45c-5d0e-bd27-517ff58902db" :question/math-academy-id "q-127920" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y=-1 \\\\ 3y-x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The lines $2x-2y=-1$ and $3y-x=1$ intersect at infinitely many  points\n- The coefficient matrix is not  invertible\n- The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not equal to zero" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is false by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127920/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127920"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32091"] :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+\\sqrt{7}y=0.3 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{0.1}x+3y=\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The lines $3x+\\sqrt{7}y=0.3$ and $-2\\sqrt{0.1}x+3y=\\sqrt{7}$ intersect exactly at one point\n- The determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $0$\n- The coefficient matrix is invertible" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the determinant cannot be $0.$\n\n- Statement III is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-127919/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "8b4dd232-a03e-56c5-88e2-830b798a0261" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127919/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ab50ef0a-1eee-5f61-834d-eb1a01bd3b03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127919/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7287c3fa-b227-53b3-b645-339e28f2a681" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127919/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "80ab4a79-1ca4-5071-a000-3e1b688e80a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127919/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "e11aa909-a283-59d3-a56e-25fc6f903f33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127919/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4909214-0fda-5fe4-85a4-b4b2ecde4990" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127919/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-127919/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-127919/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-127919/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-127919/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-127919/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127919" :question/id #uuid "353f2718-7727-57ba-8ccd-eccfc2f1f483" :question/math-academy-id "q-127919" :question/problem "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $Ax=b$ in the usual way. Given that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- $A$ is  invertible\n- $Ax=0$ has a nonzero solution" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127919/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127919"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73567/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "5a4a3a55-a4e7-5b46-938d-82a4c6b460f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73567/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "40d59a2a-3c79-554e-bdc9-d0cdc3ced487" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73567/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "3dfce005-abbc-5637-b548-91b24f305e82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73567/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c6a4d779-f1cb-537c-8f73-76eda29a68c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73567/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f601b3df-2db9-5b36-8f8e-24dbf79cbd38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73567/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "648c86d7-9fc5-5666-97b2-c82df3b75b1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73567/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-73567/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-73567/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-73567/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-73567/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-73567/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73567" :question/id #uuid "04acc9aa-31c1-5561-b4f1-2e7e780fdc1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73567" :question/problem "Let $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne 3.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $det(A)=0$\n- The lines $2x+2y=2$ and $3x+ky=0$ intersect at infinitely many points\n- $Ax=0$ has the unique solution $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot k-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2k-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $2k-6\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne 3.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the lines must intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- Statement III is true by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nFinally, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73567/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73567"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127931/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9beee2fe-0d9b-5f87-b84c-0c16c54b9a97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127931/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ad5339b2-f27d-505e-b741-e247a862fdbe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127931/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "ca03ecde-2b67-5f78-8ec4-79c7e119eb52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127931/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "afccb5f9-2048-5eee-a9b2-22c74bd43f78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127931/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9b50959f-3e57-5c3c-9472-e0c00501e730" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127931/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5effc6b-5198-558a-9d49-4c61e316403c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127931/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-127931/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-127931/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-127931/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-127931/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-127931/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127931" :question/id #uuid "747d8083-492e-5c49-bee1-5c24e423c2be" :question/math-academy-id "q-127931" :question/problem "Let $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & k\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne -3.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- $Ax=0$ has no solutions\n- The lines $x+3y=-1$ and $-x+ky=1$  intersect at exactly one point." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot k-(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $k+3\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne -3.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the unique solution to  $Ax=0$ is the trivial one (zero).\n\n- Statement III is true by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nFinally, only statements I and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127931/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127931"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47652/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "0f41ec1d-0359-576d-a936-4213aeb8f22e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47652/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "80d411a7-52a4-5ea6-8218-ffc86ebf8e4f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47652/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "34e3d74b-6136-594b-802e-6eefb223c1d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47652/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "edd2561c-4d48-5914-b112-617e4426b4bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47652/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "bbc9776a-1c7b-5b38-a903-03aa450e0c10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47652/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7fb60e92-a90c-5128-b984-b45c5f01a026" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47652/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-47652/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-47652/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-47652/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-47652/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-47652/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47652" :question/id #uuid "69f172a2-4594-5a63-9a46-4904ec33515e" :question/math-academy-id "q-47652" :question/problem "Let $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -5 & k\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne 1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- $Ax=0$ has no solution\n- The lines $5x-y=-1$ and $-5x+ky=0$ intersect exactly at one point" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -5 & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot k-(-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =5k-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $5k-5\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne 1.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, there must be a unique zero solution to $Ax=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the lines must intersect at exactly one point.\n\nFinally, only statements I and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47652/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47652"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128136/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c79b6d40-425c-5ee0-a845-a96c4c4611cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128136/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c271060b-cae4-54ba-8df4-5afcea23525e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128136/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3d9cc9b8-e1ef-55ab-9737-9bdf1487b377" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128136/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "17aee818-3d94-544e-a199-9744bcaf57e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128136/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "019b85dc-a02a-5029-88d0-dd4b07114689" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128136/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90404e8e-86e0-5ad3-aea9-f0f2fbff27fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128136/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-128136/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-128136/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-128136/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-128136/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-128136/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128136" :question/id #uuid "68d785b9-39db-5eca-8a04-698275702235" :question/math-academy-id "q-128136" :question/problem "Let $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne -4.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $det(A)=0$\n- The system  $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution\n- The lines $7x+14y=2$ and $-2x+ky=-3$ intersect at infinitely many points" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =7\\cdot k-(-2)\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =7k+28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $7k+28\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne -4.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the unique solution to $Ax=0$ is the trivial one (zero).\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the lines must intersect at exactly one point.\n\nFinally, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128136/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128136"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31919/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f974408f-71c4-5fc1-8b4a-68f76baa5054" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31919/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3c45c0d9-bca9-5aba-a30b-7b4c732cabc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31919/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e301bda0-8720-5687-aa31-5fe64f98df36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31919/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "d1b1e0ef-fc7f-5034-bca9-651831d2820a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31919/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "a2263538-23d5-5cab-8a52-d1c59366084a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/